.TH AVR\-REPO\-PUBLIC\-MIRROR\-REQUEST 1 "" "avr 0.3.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-repo-public-mirror-request \- Request a mirror of a public GitHub repository.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr repo public-mirror request
[OPTIONS] FULL_NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Request a mirror of a public GitHub repository.
.PP
FULL_NAME is the canonical GitHub owner/repository name. Avrea validates the repository with GitHub before recording the request.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr repo public-mirror request rust-lang/rust
    avr repo public-mirror request rust-lang/rust --reason "Build dependency"
    avr repo public-mirror request rust-lang/rust --org acme --json '*'
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    approval_state, created_at, github_snapshot, public_access_expires_at,
    reason, repository_full_name, repository_id, request_id,
    requester_organization_id, requester_user_id, review_note, reviewed_at,
    reviewed_by_user_id, status, updated_at
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIFULL_NAME\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fITEXT\fR
Why your organization needs this repository mirrored.
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-repo-public-mirror (1),
.BR avr-repo-public-mirror-cancel (1),
.BR avr-repo-public-mirror-check (1),
.BR avr-repo-public-mirror-requests (1),
.BR avr-repo-public-mirror-view (1)
